## Key Learning

Application startup delays are not always caused by resource constraints or application defects. A systematic troubleshooting approach—starting 
with infrastructure validation, followed by application log analysis and dependency verification—helps isolate subtle configuration issues. 
In this incident, a missing hostname entry caused repeated name resolution timeouts, significantly delaying application initialization despite 
the underlying operating system being healthy.



